 "poem": "183, The Commencement of the Composition of\nI. Adieu! Some Maidens have departed\nLike stars; but all are fair to me above.\nWho would ask what manner of beauty\nAre these whom I have seen in life's early\nDay? 'Tis not that which canst thou claim alone,\nThat beauty which rises from soul alone,\nOr which cannot be without several own,\nBut that which canst boast and its beauty.\nII. Let each my fancy send away\nThe scenes that fill it with a glowing ray.\nWhat were its charm, could it bring again",
